(1227,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF00P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF97 at epoch 2000.40. Realized by a frame of 31 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to February 2000. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2000-05-26',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','DGF00P01 is included in ITRF2000 as a regional densification for South America. Replaced by DGF01P01 (datum code 1228).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1228,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF01P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF2000 at epoch 2000.00. Realized by a frame of 48 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to April 2001. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2000-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF00P01 (datum code 1227). Replaced by DGF01P02 (datum code 1229).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1229,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF01P02','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF2000 at epoch 1998.40. Realized by a frame of 49 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to October 2001. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','1998-05-26',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF01P01 (datum code 1228). Replaced by DGF02P01 (datum code 1230).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1230,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF02P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF2000 at epoch 2000.00. Realized by a frame of 53 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to July 2002. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2000-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF01P02 (datum code 1229). Replaced by DGF04P01 (datum code 1331).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1231,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF04P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF2000 at epoch 2003.00. Realized by a frame of 69 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to July 2004. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2003-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF02P01 (datum code 1230). Replaced by DGF05P01 (datum code 1232).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1232,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF05P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF2000 at epoch 2004.00. Realized by a frame of 95 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to September 2005. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2004-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF04P01 (datum code 1231). Replaced by DGF06P01 (datum code 1233).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1233,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF06P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF2000 at epoch 2004.00. Realized by a frame of 94 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from June 1996 to June 2006. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2004-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF05P01 (datum code 1232). Replaced by DGF07P01 (datum code 1234).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1234,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF07P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGS05 at epoch 2004.50. Realized by a frame of 106 continuously operating stations using GPS observations in 3 periods between December 2001 and October 2007. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2004-07-02',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF06P01 (datum code 1233). Replaced by DGF08P01 (datum code 1235).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1235,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network DGF08P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGS05 at epoch 2004.50. Realized by a frame of 126 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from December 2002 to March 2008. Velocity model VEMOS2003 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2004-07-02',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF07P01 (datum code 1234). Replaced by SIR09P01  (datum code 1236).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1236,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR09P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGS05 at epoch 2005.00. Realized by a frame of 128 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from January 2000 to January 2009. Velocity model VEMOS2009 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2005-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces DGF08P01 (datum code 1235). Replaced by SIR10P01 (datum code 1237).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1237,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR10P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF08 at epoch 2005.00. Realized by a frame of 183 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from January 2000 to June 2010. Velocity model VEMOS2009 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2005-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces SIR09P01 (datum code 1236). Replaced by SIR11P01 (datum code 1238).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1238,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR11P01','geodetic','Aligned to ITRF08 at epoch 2005.00. Realized by a frame of 230 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from January 2000 to April 2011. Velocity model VEMOS2009 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2005-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces SIR10P01 (datum code 1237). Replaced by SIR13P01 (datum code 1239). Last multi-year solution without the effects of the El Maule earthquake in February 2010.','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1239,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR13P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGb08 at epoch 2012.00. Realized by a frame of 108 continuously operating stations using GPS observations from April 2010 to June 2013. Velocity model VEMOS2009 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2012-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces SIR11P01 (datum code 1238). Replaced by SIR14P01 (datum code 1240). First multi-year solution after the El Maule earthquake of February 2010.','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1240,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR14P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGb08 at epoch 2013.00. Realized by a frame of 242 continuously operating stations using GNSS observations from April 2010 to July 2014. Velocity model VEMOS2009 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2013-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces SIR13P01 (datum code 1239). Replaced by SIR15P01 (datum code 1241).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1241,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR15P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGb08 at epoch 2013.00. Realized by a frame of 303 continuously operating stations using GNSS observations from March 2010 to April 2015. Velocity model VEMOS2015 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2013-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces SIR14P01 (datum code 1240). Replaced by SIR17P01 (datum code 1242).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1242,'SIRGAS Continuously Operating Network SIR17P01','geodetic','Aligned to IGS14 at epoch 2015.00. Realized by a frame of 345 continuously operating stations using GNSS observations from April 2011 to January 2017. Velocity model VEMOS2017 used to propagate coordinates to the frame reference epoch.','2015-01-01',7019,8901,4530,'Geodetic survey.','Replaces SIR15P01 (datum code 1241).','SIRGAS web site www.sirgas.org and ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-04-11','2019.020',false),
(1244,'IGS97','geodetic','Derived from ITRF97 at epoch 1997.00 through a subset of stable IGS station coordinates. Preserves the ITRF origin, orientation and scale, but without any distortions introduced from non-GNSS space-geodetic techniques.','1997-01-01',7019,8901,1262,'Geodesy. GPS satellite ephemerides produced by US NGS and other International GNSS Service (IGS) analysis centres are expressed in this datum.','Used for IGS products from GPS week 1065 through GPS week 1142 (2000-06-04 to 2001-12-01). Replaced by IGS00. For all practical purposes coincident with ITRF97.','http://www.ngs.noaa.gov/CORS/','IOGP','2019-05-15','2019.031',false),
(1245,'IGS00','geodetic','Derived from ITRF2000 at epoch 1998.00 through a subset of 54 stable IGS station coordinates. Preserves the ITRF origin, orientation and scale, but without any distortions introduced from non-GNSS space-geodetic techniques.','1998-01-01',7019,8901,1262,'Geodesy.','Used for IGS products from GPS week 1143 through GPS week 1252 (2001-12-02 through 2004-01-10). Replaces IGS97, replaced by IGb00. For all practical purposes coincident with ITRF2000.','International GNSS Service (IGS) via ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-05-10','2019.031',false),
(1246,'IGb00','geodetic','Derived from ITRF2000 at epoch 1998.00 through a subset of 99 stable IGS station coordinates. Preserves the ITRF origin, orientation and scale, but without any distortions introduced from non-GNSS space-geodetic techniques.','1998-01-01',7019,8901,1262,'Geodesy. GPS satellite ephemerides produced by US NGS and other International GNSS Service (IGS) analysis centres are expressed in this datum.','Used for IGS products from GPS week 1253 through GPS week 1399 (2004-01-11 to 2006-11-04). Replaces IGS00, replaced by IGS05. For all practical purposes coincident with ITRF2000.','International GNSS Service (IGS) via ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-05-15','2019.031',false),
(1247,'IGS05','geodetic','Derived from ITRF2005 at epoch 2000.00 through a subset of 139 stable IGS station coordinates. Preserves the ITRF origin, orientation and scale, but without any distortions introduced from non-GNSS space-geodetic techniques.','2000-01-01',7019,8901,1262,'Geodesy.','Used for IGS products from GPS week 1400 through GPS week 1631 (2006-11-05 to 2011-04-16). Replaces IGb00, replaced by IGb08. For all practical purposes coincident with ITRF2005.','International GNSS Service (IGS) via ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-05-14','2019.031',false),
(1248,'IGb08','geodetic','Derived from ITRF2008 at epoch 2005.00 through a subset of 232 stable IGS station coordinates. Preserves the ITRF origin, orientation and scale, but without any distortions introduced from non-GNSS space-geodetic techniques.','2005-01-01',7019,8901,1262,'Geodesy.','Used for IGS products from GPS week 1709 through GPS week 1933 (2012-10-07 to 2017-01-28). Replaces IGS08, replaced by IGS14. For all practical purposes coincident with ITRF2008.','International GNSS Service (IGS) via ISO Geodetic Registry.','IOGP','2019-05-10','2019.031',false),
(1250,'IGN 2008 LD','vertical','Mean sea level at Pointe-à-Pitre. Origin = IGN Marker 20A with defined height of 0.50 m above msl of 1987.','2008-01-01',Null,Null,2893,'Geodetic survey, topographic mapping, engineering survey.','Orthometric heights. Replaces IGN 1992 LD (datum code 5212).','IGN Paris','IOGP','2019-05-30','2019.043',false),
(1251,'Kosovo Reference System 2001','geodetic','Densification of ETRF97 in Kosovo at epoch 2001.25.','2001-04-01',7019,8901,4542,'Geodesy.','First order network of 32 stations connected to 8 EUREF Permanant Network (EPN) stations observed march-April 2001. Densified in 2012.','Kosovo Cadastral Agency (KCA).','IOGP','2019-07-16','2019.042',false),
(5100,'Mean Sea Level','vertical','The average height of the surface of the sea at a tide station for all stages of the tide over a 19-year period, usually determined from hourly height readings measured from a fixed predetermined reference level.','',Null,Null,1262,'Hydrography.','Approximates geoid. Users are advised to not use this generic vertical datum but to define explicit realizations of MSL by specifying location and epoch, for instance "MSL at xxx during yyyy-yyyy".','IHO Dictionary, S-32, 5th Edition, 3156.','IOGP','2017-07-14','2011.047 2017.029',false),
