(6326,'World Geodetic System 1984','geodetic','Defined through a consistent set of station coordinates. These have changed with time: by 0.7m on 1994-06-29 (G730), a further 0.2m on 1997-01-29 (G873),  0.06m on 2002-01-20 (G1150), 0.2m on 2012-02-08 (G1674) and 0.02m on 2013-10-16 (G1762).','',7030,8901,1262,'Satellite navigation.','EPSG::6326 has been the then current realization. No distinction is made between the original and subsequent (G730, G873, G1150, G1674 and G1762) WGS 84 frames. Since 1997, WGS 84 has been maintained within 10cm of the then current ITRF.','NIMA TR8350.2 June 2004 revision. http://earth-info.nga.mil/GandG/publications/tr8350.2/tr8350_2.html and ¶http://gis-lab.info/docs/nima-tr8350.2-addendum.pdf. Also NGA.STND.0036_1.0.0_WGS84 of 2014-07-08.','IOGP','2017-07-14','2002.151 2002.890 2003.270 2005.460 2005.550 2006.810 2012.097 2014.081 2017.029',false),
